---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<section id="install" class="install-section" data-section="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
  <div class="reading-container centered-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Quick start</p>
    <h2 id="install-heading">Install Comis on your infrastructure.</h2>
    <p class="lead">One-line managed install for macOS and Linux.</p>

    <div class="command-panel">
      <div class="command-line" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="One-line installer command">
        <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
        <code id="install-command" data-install-command>{SITE.installCommand}</code>
      </div>
      <button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy-button hidden>
        <span data-copy-label>Copy command</span>
      </button>
      <p class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-copy-status></p>
    </div>

    <p>
      This command downloads and runs the installer immediately.
    </p>
    <p>
      The managed-host path can install Node.js and host dependencies, initialize Comis data, and register the daemon with systemd or PM2. On Linux, it also attempts to provision Chromium and Xvfb by default and can create a dedicated <code>comis</code> user for a systemd service. Run <code>bash comis-install.sh --help</code> to review opt-outs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer to inspect it first? Download it with <code>curl -fsSL --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 https://comis.ai/install.sh -o comis-install.sh</code>, review it with <code>less comis-install.sh</code>, preview changes with <code>bash comis-install.sh --dry-run</code>, then run <code>bash comis-install.sh</code> when ready.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer a smaller footprint? With Node.js 22.19 or newer, run <code>npm install --global comisai</code>, followed by <code>comis init</code>. The npm path does not install host tools, create a service account, or register a service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Complete setup, start the daemon if prompted, then open <code>http://127.0.0.1:4766</code>. Linux with Bubblewrap is the recommended deployment target for isolated tool execution.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link standalone-link" href={SITE.installationDocs}>View all installation options</a>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline type="module" src="/copy-command.js"></script>
